  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">GENDEV - buy-in ID - World Bank Group&#x2019;s Invest in Childcare Initiative</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">(USAID Bureau for Inclusive Growth, Partnerships, and Innovation (IPI)):  The World Bank Invest in Childcare Initiative is designed to expand the size and improve the quality of World Bank (WB)  investments in childcare, thereby improving women&apos;s economic empowerment and child development outcomes, and yielding broader benefits for families, businesses, and economies. The ID Hub supports management of the initiative, which advances care infrastructure, one of the four key lines of effort of the US Strategy on Global Women&apos;s Economic Security.  Starting in 2022, USAID made a commitment of $50 million over five years to the initiative. The Agency&apos;s funding is critical in coordinating and creating public-private partnerships that aim to invest at least $180 million over five years to expand accessible, affordable, and high-quality care services. In the first year, $53 million -$25 million in grant funding, which was matched with $23 million in WB funding- in total childcare investment was possible because of USAID, to date, 14 countries (C&amp;ocirc;te d&apos;Ivoire, Ethiopia, Ghana, Indonesia, Jordan, Kosovo, Kyrgyz Republic, Moldova, Rwanda, Senegal, Somalia, Tanzania, Ukraine, and Uzbekistan) have received grants. Most recently, Italy committed &amp;euro;12 million inspired by USAID&apos;s engagement. To ensure continued progress and meet the USG/USAID commitment, GenDev will allocate $10 million in FY24 funding.</narrative>
  </description>
